# What the Vercel CLI may upload.
#
# The project's Root Directory is `apps/mobile`, but the CLI uploads the
# directory it is run from — and it has to run from here, or it resolves the
# root directory twice. So the upload is whitelisted: the app, and from it
# only what the build reads. Everything else — the Go services, the contracts,
# the indexer, local notes and env files — stays on the machine.
#
# This file replaces .gitignore for the upload: once it exists, .gitignore is
# not consulted, so every heavy or private path has to be named here.

/*
!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/mobile

# Local secrets and machine-specific values. EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build
# time, so an uploaded .env would bake a laptop's address into the site.
/apps/mobile/.env
/apps/mobile/.env.*
!/apps/mobile/.env.example

# Native projects, dependencies, build output, tests: the web build needs none
# of them.
/apps/mobile/node_modules
/apps/mobile/ios
/apps/mobile/android
/apps/mobile/dist
/apps/mobile/.expo
/apps/mobile/e2e
/apps/mobile/test-results
/apps/mobile/playwright-report
